    "name": "Organic Blue Cornmeal",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Blue cornmeal is&nbsp;a nutritious, earthy-flavored flour from ground blue corn, rich in antioxidants (</span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=anthocyanins&amp;sca_esv=a48d1260c77b0e92&amp;rlz=1CAVNCX_enUS1049US1049&amp;sxsrf=ANbL-n45bpJmtpk3Kjboi6AYSdSxpjp7Hg%3A1769105862823&amp;ei=xmlyaeL8MZu90PEPxbL1-QQ&amp;oq=blue+cornmeal+info&amp;gs_&amp;sclient=gws-wiz-serp&amp;mstk=AUtExfB4VOrDEoBtQrpZ_ONwvnZDZOp1T_wAcAtWe0XhE31AE83OCER_Pi324u-u5T9fzjlJjBcsP78PHMuvH1Q6iRYdJjq945DPSXMpAYJQDtNf-J2MchLEm4fYe9L6giAECIgOQuY9yiEEJgzUvrvoVWp8qe8uo6tB_og2UUI8i6HTpV_fOMfIIIPgVfIwH0G4Qhszq0iD7t_oc8sKm3D2ITvCappF2pXQu6FXI7onmMptKIlkl-U1ESkYjcAMKXpRlF7Bq_ra2RRrmRPcs4TZapej&amp;csui=3&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiquO_44J-SAxUfKzQIHQGBGgEQgK4QegQIARAE\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">anthocyanins</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">) and protein, used by Native Americans for tortillas, breads, and mush, offering a nutty taste and vibrant color for baking, thickening, or breading, with benefits like lower glycemic impact than yellow corn. It's naturally gluten-free, adds texture, and can substitute regular cornmeal in recipes.&nbsp;</span></p>",
